| F5 | open | IMPORTANT | js/smAgent.js | ⚠️ important iocachettlms re raise registry f3 — re introduced the claimed fix is not on the branch round 1 finding answered in the registry as re introduced the round 1 thread asked for the knob or a description amend the rework lap did neither — and the author reply claiming the fix does not hold at the reviewed head new evidence at head 33a890d4 the reply cites wired in js common smprovider js jobparams tuning lines 118–119 — smprovider js 118 119 is the inside of iocachecollect a key prefix loop over cache entries it contains no jobparams code and git log 05333273 head js common smprovider js is empty — no commit in the rework touched that file the only ttl in the tree remains the hardcoded sm io cache ttl ms 60 1000 js common smprovider js 74 75 frozen pre pr line repo wide grep rni iocachettlms js json docs → zero hits the pr description updated 2026 11 18t05 06 input pr 1514 pr info md 21 ticket md 9 still promises iocachettlms jobparam exposes the io cache ttl 60s default unchanged only liveprobettlms is wired this line applyprobetuning either expose the knob for real — accept iocachettlms from jobparams and feed smprovider s io cache ttl the same way applyprobetuning feeds the probe layer — or amend the pr description so the stated contract matches the shipped diff as written an operator following the description cannot tune the io cache ttl |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

